#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions and Answers"

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>What is &amarok;?</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>What is &amarok;?</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; is a music player for Unix systems (eg. Linux). More information can "
"be found in a <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/What_is_amaroK%3F\">"
"summary of its features</ulink> and the <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/index.php?set_albumName=Screenshots&amp;option=com_g"
"allery&amp;Itemid=60&amp;include=view_album.php\">screenshot gallery</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use &amarok; without KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; only requires KDElibs, none of the other KDE stuff. So you have to "
"have KDElibs installed properly (including all the binaries that come with it, "
"as &amarok; needs some of these to find plugins and for the script plugins). We "
"have written an entry for <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/KDElibs_without_aRts\">"
"how to compile a minimal KDElibs</ulink>, which you may find useful."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For some features to work correctly, such as the on-screen display, require "
"your window manager to support the relevant freedesktop.org standards. So GNOME "
"will work well, but fluxbox will have some trouble. We are committed to "
"supporting &amarok; on all platforms. We use KDElibs and Qt because they "
"provide an excellent development environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; crashes during the Collection scan, always at the same point. What's "
"happenning?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's likely that one file in your Collection triggers a bug in the TagLib "
"library, and makes &amarok; crash. You can identify this file by looking at "
"~/.kde/share/apps/amarok/collection_scan.log. You should report this crash to "
"the TagLib bug database on <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/\">"
"bugs.kde.org</ulink> and attach the broken file. Afterward you can remove the "
"file from your Collection and repeat the scanning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; crashes when I play a certain track, everytime, what's wrong?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This usually means TagLib is crashing while reading that track's tags. Report "
"the bug against TagLib at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/\">"
"bugs.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; crashes often, what can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Upgrade your ALSA libs and utils to the latest version, or use OSS, or OSS "
"emulation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use MySQL as the database backend, try the SQLite one, it is slightly "
"more mature (the &amarok; code, not the db itself)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Try a different audio-engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure that all the libraries that &amarok; uses were compiled with the same "
"GCC version as &amarok; itself. The situation when &amarok; is compiled using "
"GCC 3.4.x and linked against taglib which was compiled using GCC 3.3.x can lead "
"to crashes during tag editing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you're using KDE with artsd, try disabling \"auto suspend if idle after...\" "
"in the sound system settings or at least don't use a value of 1 second since "
"that will interfere every time amarok switches songs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Otherwise, forward us the backtraces when the email pops-up (you'll see). If "
"you get a crash often you will get it fixed for sure if you forward a really "
"good backtrace to us. See the next sections for assistance there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I obtain a decent backtrace?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/Debugging_HowTo\">"
"Debugging HowTo</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; is not using the tags I know are in my files!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If Konqueror or other apps are displaying different Title, Artist, Album or "
"Genre information than &amarok; is picking up when it creates your collection, "
"it may be reading the older ID3v1 format tags rather than the newer ID3v2 tags. "
"This can be due to your <guilabel>Encodings</guilabel> "
"setting: Go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Configure &amarok;</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, and then find the Encodings "
"section of the Settings panel. Uncheck all checkboxes to \"Do not decode the "
"following as latin1\". Rescan your collection to pick up the ID3v2 tags."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; is not displaying my utf-8 id3v2 tags properly!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is because most applications put utf8 data into id3v2 tags but do not "
"specify the encoding as unicode. This perl script will fix that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: faq.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#!/usr/bin/perl\n"
"die \"File $ARGV[0] doesn't exist\" unless -f $ARGV[0];\n"
"use MP3::Mplib;\n"
"my $mp3 = MP3::Mplib->new($ARGV[0]);\n"
"my $v2tag = $mp3->get_v2tag;\n"
"print \"Error writing tags of $ARGV[0]\\n\" unless $mp3->"
"set_v2tag($v2tag,&amp;UTF8);"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This script requires the perl module MP3::Mplib which can be installed by "
"issuing this command <command>perl -MCPAN -e 'install MP3::Mplib'</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why do my statusbar icons always look active?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; statusbar icons(Random/Repeat/Append) look constantly Active on KDE "
"3.4.0. This is a known bug in KDE 3.4.0. The icon effects are sometimes "
"forgotten. Simple fix kcontrol <menuchoice><guimenu>Appearance</guimenu>"
"<guisubmenu>Icons</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Advanced</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
", set disabled state to \"Gray\" and \"Semi-transparent\". Note that sometimes "
"you must click on the icon 3 times before it has an effect after making this "
"change."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why does &amarok; complain about undefined symbols and then refuses to start?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if you get this error : \"amarokapp: symbol lookup error: amarokapp: undefined "
"symbol: _ZN11KSystemTray9setPixmapERK7QPixmap\", then check that amarokapp uses "
"the correct libqt (check with : ldd `which amarokapp` | grep qt)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To fix it, you might have to remove any conflicting libqt and/or edit "
"/etc/ld.so.conf so it pick up the correct version first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Useage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get support for &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several options. Often times problems you have with the initial "
"install of &amarok; are best answered by experts of your particular Unix or "
"Linux distribution. You may seek help from fellow users and developers at the "
"<ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/index.php?option=com_simpleboard\">"
"&amarok; forum</ulink> and the <ulink url=\"irc://irc.freenode.net/amarok\">"
"IRC channel</ulink> at irc.freenode.net channel #amarok."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org\">Bugzilla</ulink> is not a place to seek "
"support. Please do enter a bug if you are serious about helping fix a bug in "
"&amarok; itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I start &amarok;, I see an empty playlist. How do I actually get tracks in "
"there?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simple. Use the File Browser on the left side to navigate to the desired "
"directory. Then drag the files into the Playlist part on the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I remove tracks from the Playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the files you want to remove, and press Del key on your keyboard. Or "
"right-click the selection and choose Remove Selected from pop up menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I load a playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just drag and drop the playlist file into the Playlist, like you would do with "
"any other file. It's that simple!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I save the current playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Save playlist button is next to Add Media button in the Playlist Toolbar. "
"Just click it!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are no visualizations in the visualizations dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You probably don't have xmms-config installed, reconfigure and build after "
"installing the appropriate xmms-devel package. You also may want to install the "
"latest version of <ulink url=\"http://libvisual.sourceforge.net/v2/\">"
"libvisual</ulink>, which has some ultra fancy visualizations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where's the equalizer?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Equalizer Window can be found in the right mouse button menu. You can also "
"find it in the Menubar by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Equalizer</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playback"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "What media types does &amarok; support?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"None. Yes, that's right! None! We have a backend independent approach, so the "
"question you should be asking is \"What media types does "
"GStreamer/xine/aRts/NMM/MAS/KDEmm support?\" So as you can guess we pretty much "
"support absolutely every audio format you can think of. GStreamer can even "
"decode text and PNG!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information, have a look at <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/Audio_Engine_Comparison\">"
"Audio Engine Comparison</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why can't &amarok; play MP3s?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It can! Chances are you're using Fedora/RedHat linux, they don't ship with MP3 "
"decoders by default (due to patenting issues). Solution: Alt-F2, gg:redhat mp3 "
"kde, ENTER"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; won't play MP3's under SUSE Linux 9.3, what could I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the \"YaST Online Update\" and install the 'Multimedia Option Pack 1' "
"patch. Voila, &amarok; plays MP3's."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With GStreamer-engine I'm getting 100% CPU usage while playing. How can I fix "
"it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When using GStreamer-engine with alsasink, &amarok; requires the device to "
"provide a mixer. Mixing allows multiple applications to access the device at "
"the same time, and output sound simultaneously. This can either be achieved by "
"using a soundcard with hardware-mixing (e.g. SBLive), or by using the \"dmix\" "
"plugin for alsa, which provides software-mixing. See <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/Setting_up_Dmix_for_ALSA\">"
"Setting up Dmix for ALSA</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After installation you need to specify \"dmix\" as the sound device in the "
"engine settings dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "I can't get any media to play in &amarok;, why not?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "You need to test the sound frameworks at the commandline:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>artsplay foobar.mp3</command> <command>gst-launch filesrc "
"location=/home/foo/bar.mp3 ! spider ! audioscale ! audioconvert ! "
"alsasink</command> <command>xine-check</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The output from these commands should help you identify the problems you are "
"having and how to fix them. Please note you may need to use a different sink to "
"test GStreamer (eg. osssink)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can &amarok; output directly to OSS/ALSA?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We already do! Don't forget that the media must be decoded first! You can't "
"just pipe an MP3 to ALSA, all you will get is white-noise. GStreamer is the "
"best choice for most people who want a low-overhead decoding solution, it reads "
"the file, decodes it and pipes the PCM data to ALSA. Exactly like XMMS."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "But! XMMS can output directly to ALSA!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"But it decodes it first! GStreamer can output directly to ALSA too! So can "
"xine!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "The sound stutters, is there anything I can do to improve it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can either use the GStreamer engine (it's great!), or tweak aRts. Open "
"Control Center <menuchoice><guimenu>Sound and Multimedia</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Sound System</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Enable Run with highest possible "
"priority, and increase the size of the Sound buffer: (warning, see the next "
"FAQ!) You should also ensure that your artswrapper is suid:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>su</command> <command>chmod a+rsx "
"/path/to/kde/bin/artswrapper</command> <command>killall -9 artsd</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With KDE 3.2.x there are issues with the KDEMultimedia codecs that can cause "
"distorted playback, please see <ulink "
"url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=80497\">this bug report</ulink>"
". Also, increasing the size of the sound buffer in your .asoundrc alsa "
"configuration file can help a great deal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "The CPU usage is high, is there anything I can do to improve it?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Either don't use the aRts-engine, use the GStreamer or xine engines, or address "
"the high CPU usage by installing KDEMultimedia in its entirety to get the "
"faster aRts codecs (eg. libarts_mpeglib.so, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &amarok; analyzers are really unresponsive!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are probably using the aRts-engine, either use another engine (the "
"xine-engine has been seriously tweaked to give perfect analyzer-sync), or "
"reduce the size of your aRts buffer in kcontrol, sound system. The lower the "
"buffer the more responsive the visuals. Yes this is a bug, please help us fix "
"it!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have GStreamer installed but when I try to change to the GStreamer engine "
"&amarok; crashes, what gives?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After installing GStreamer you have register it's components, running "
"`gst-register` (sometimes suffixed with a version, so gst-register-0.8) should "
"take care of registering your GStreamer components."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I ran gst-register but I still have have GStreamer troubles, what can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can try the <ulink "
"url=\"http://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/data/doc/gstreamer/head/faq/html/chapter-"
"using.html\">GStreamer FAQ</ulink>. If all else fails you can try the "
"knowledgeable people at the <ulink url=\"irc://irc.freenode.net/gstreamer\">"
"#gstreamer IRC channel</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; says that the GStreamer engine cannot play MP3 files, although I have "
"compiled/installed the mad plugin!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try this (make sure that &amarok; does not run): - <ulink "
"url=\"http://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/src/gst-ffmpeg/\">Download</ulink>"
", compile and install the ffmpeg package - Run gst-register (you may need to "
"run it twice, as root and as your \"normal\" user) - Go to your GStreamer "
"plugin directory (you can find it with gst-config / gstreamer-config) - Delete "
"the ffmpeg files (or move them somewhere else) - Run gst-register again - Start "
"&amarok;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Development"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get a cvs/svn version of &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: faq.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to obtain and build SVN &amarok;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "I've found a bug / I've got a great idea for &amarok;!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please report it at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/\">bugs.kde.org</ulink>"
", if you have a list of suggestions/wishes it may be best to send them to our "
"mailing list: <email>amarok-devel@lists.sourceforge.net</email>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do you accept patches?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Happily! Your best course of action is to let us know what you plan to do "
"before you do any work so we can discuss it, but don't fret we haven't turned "
"down a patch yet! Discussion is mostly to help you patch the correct bits of "
"&amarok;. Then either submit a patch to the mailing list, or commit if you have "
"svn access. However, please let us know before you commit new features to svn! "
"If you have a bug fix then just go ahead, this is open source after all :)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why did you choose the name &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; is an album by British composer Mike Oldfield. I happen to like it a "
"lot, and I think the name's got a nice sound. Plus, of course, it contains the "
"all important “K”.. :)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid "Is it &amarok;, AmaroK or Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is &amarok;! Yes, we understand this is unconventional ;-)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tips and Tricks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I use &amarok; as an alarm clock?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actually, thanks to the magic of DCOP you already can :) Simply set an alarm in "
"your favorite calendar program and tell it to run the following command: "
"<command>dcop amarok player play</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command will tell &amarok; to start playing. Make sure that &amarok; is "
"running before you go to bed, and you should wake up to the merry tune of "
"whatever you pressed stop on before going to bed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I get what &amarok; is playing right now, when I'm on another computer?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a properly set up ssh environment, you can use that to get the "
"information. The following command will return the Now Playing string. <command>"
"ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_rsa yourip dcop --user yourusername amarok player "
"nowPlaying</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure that you replace yourip with your IP and yourusername with your "
"username. Also note that this expects your identification to be found in the "
"~/.ssh/id_rsa file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid "What kind of tricks can the Player Window do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &amarok; player analyzers can be detached from the Player Window. By "
"pressing d on your keyboard the active analyzer will open in an independent, "
"re-sizeable window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "What kind of tricks can the Playlist Window do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Holding Control and clicking the right mouse button enqueues files in the order "
"in which you clicked them. Pressing Enter after making a playlist search will "
"play the first search item and will clear the search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I see the Player Window and Playlist Window have neat tricks, what about the "
"tray icon?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hovering your mouse on the icon will display a nice popup with current track "
"information. Clicking the middle mouse button on the icon play-pauses the "
"current track. Scrolling the mouse wheel changes volume. Holding Shift while "
"scrolling the mouse wheel seeks through the current track. Holding Control "
"while scrolling the mouse wheel will skip through tracks in the playlist. "
"Dragging and dropping items into the tray icon opens a pop up menu allowing you "
"to choose from three options, Append to Playlist, Append and Play, and Queue "
"after Current Track. Tray icon is also a song position indicator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I find the settings for amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.kde/share/apps/amarok ~/.kde/share/config/amarokrc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid "How Do I use an external MySQL database with &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/MySQL_HowTo\">"
"MySQL HowTo</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"My $HOME is located on NFS. After startup, &amarok; fails to build the "
"Collection, printing many database errors to the console. What to do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The internal SQLite database which &amarok; uses by default does not work on "
"NFS. You must either link your ~/.kde/share/apps/amarok directory to a local "
"drive, or use the MySQL support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I rip/encode Audio-CDs with &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert your CD, then click on \"Play Audio CD\" in the menu. The File-Browser "
"will come up and show a tree with several folders. For normal ripping, go to "
"the \"wav\" folder, select some tracks and drag them to the desired destination "
"in a Konqueror window. For automatic encoding, drag files from the \"mp3\" or "
"\"ogg\" folder instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"CD-ripping requires the \"AudioCD KIO-slave\" to be installed. It is part of "
"KDE-Multimedia."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "How are track ratings determined?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; assigns a rating (a number 1-100) to a song based on how many times "
"you've listened to it and whether you skip the song without it finishing. Every "
"time the song finishes playing, the rating is changed. The code for changing "
"the rating is in collectiondb.cpp. As of version 1.2.2, it was on line 1181, "
"though you can find it by searching for \"CollectionDB::addSongPercentage\". "
"When defining a score for a track which has never been played before, &amarok; "
"uses the calculation score = ( ( 50 + percentage ) / 2 )"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets the score equal to a number from 25-75, depending on how far through "
"the song was allowed to play. For example, if the user stops or skips the song "
"after only 25% of it has played, the score will be set to (50+25)/2, or 37.5. "
"Scores are displayed as integers, however, so this number is rounded to the "
"nearest integer before being displayed. The score is kept internally as a "
"floating point number however, since after a song has been played several "
"times, it may be impossible to alter the score by more than a point with a "
"single play (see below). When defining a score for a track which has been "
"played before, the calculation is a bit more complicated. In the source, it is "
"score = ( ( values[2].toDouble() * values.first().toInt() ) + percentage ) / ( "
"values.first().toInt() + 1 );"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "Substituting in the values from this line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: faq.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"QStringList values = query( QString(\n"
"           \"SELECT playcounter, createdate, percentage FROM statistics \"\n"
"           \"WHERE url = '%1';\" )\n"
"           .arg( escapeString( url ) ) );"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We have score = ( ( statistics_percentage.toDouble() * PlayCounter.toInt() ) + "
"percentage ) / ( PlayCounter.toInt() + 1 );"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Basically, this adjusts the previous score (statistics_percentage) by a "
"decreasing amount depending on how many times the track has been played. The "
"more times the track has been played, the less of an impact each play has on "
"the score."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I manually change a track's rating?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may change the rating manually by right-clicking on the playlist columns "
"titles (the ones that say title, artist, album etc) and select Score. You can "
"then change the score like any other song attribute, by right clicking it and "
"selecting \"Edit Tag 'Score'\" or pressing F2. You can also edit the score in "
"the Tag dialog, available by right clicking on a track."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why isn't &amarok; part of KDEmultimedia?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The developers don't want the man telling them when they can release. (Meaning, "
"packages in KDE proper have a release schedule that doesn't fit with &amarok;'s "
"fast-paced development)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I prevent the &amarok; icon from blinking in my system tray?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a new feature that has been added that some users might find "
"distracting. Simply uncheck the \"Flash icon tray when playing\" option under "
"General Options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I show/remove the analyzer in the playlist window?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The playlist analyzer is part of the playlist toolbar. Select <menuchoice>"
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice> Add/Remove Analyzer to the Current actions Press OK"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I change the Context Browser theme?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Download a <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/Themes\">"
"theme</ulink> or make your <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/CSS_Styles\">own</ulink>"
". Install it through <menuchoice><guimenu>Configure &amarok;... </guimenu>"
"<guisubmenu>Appearance</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Context Browser "
"Style</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, click Install New Style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid "What legal issues caused \"Blue Wolf\" icon replacement?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:697
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The icon was way too similar to the Warp Graphics, Inc. logo (elfquest.com), so "
"it had to be removed to avoid problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid "I don't have any visualizations. Where can I obtain these ?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:708
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Install the latest version of <ulink url=\"http://libvisual.sf.net\">"
"libvisual</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:715
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I add my favorite streams to &amarok;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:719
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First of all, load the stream into the playlist. There are several ways to do "
"this. You can simply click on a Stream-Playlist URL in Konqueror; &amarok; will "
"then automatically open the stream. E.g. on <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.shoutcast.com\">shoutcast.com</ulink>"
", click on the \"Tune In\" button. Or you can use the \"Add Media\" function to "
"load a stream.Once the stream is loaded, you can save it by right-clicking on "
"\"Current Playlist\" in the Playlist-Browser, then select \"Save\", and give it "
"a meaningful name. The Stream will then be added to the Playlist-Browser view "
"for later reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid "Konqueror Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is Konqueror Sidebar?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Konqueror sidebar allows you to monitor/control &amarok; while browsing with "
"Konqueror. To see it, run Konqueror, press F9 to see sidebar, click on "
"preferences (top one) button, in dropdown menu choose <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Add</guimenu> <guimenuitem>&amarok; Konqueror Sidebar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid "Audioscrobbler"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is Audioscrobbler?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Audioscrobbler is a free service that is sends information regarding which "
"songs are played to an independent server. The service signup is free and only "
"requires that you pick a user name and password that is not already in use. "
"Audioscrobbler is currently utilized in &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:770
#, no-c-format
msgid "I do not want &amarok; to send information to Audioscrobbler!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Uncheck \"Submit tracks I play\" to prevent querying Audioscrobbler for "
"suggested tracks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get to the Audioscrobbler &amarok; group?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:785
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Audioscrobbler &amarok; group is located here: <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.audioscrobbler.com/group/amaroK+users/\">"
"&amarok; Audioscrobbler Group</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Engine/Playback Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid "Which sound engine should I use?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please refer to the <ulink "
"url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/amarokwiki/index.php/Audio_Engine_Comparison\">"
"Audio Engine Comparison</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:814
#, no-c-format
msgid "What version of ALSA should I use?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:818
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you output to ALSA, you should use the newest available version of ALSA "
"possible! Old versions of ALSA have caused plenty of crashes, and have caused "
"plenty of wrongly attributed crash-reports."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:825
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I've installed GStreamer/xine/etc., but the relevant audio-engine won't show "
"up. What gives?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; was probably compiled before you had xine and/or gstreamer installed, "
"so the ./configure routine did not include them in the list of engines to be "
"built. You will have to rebuild &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:836
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"But I did rebuild &amarok; after installing gstreamer and/or xine, but the "
"engine still does not show up. What happened?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You most likely are using a distro that packages development libraries "
"separately from the main library, so even though gstreamer is installed, "
"&amarok; cannot link to it because gstreamer-devel is not installed. The same "
"issue exists for xine, you must install xine-devel if your distro splits "
"packages in this fashion. Don't forget to rebuild &amarok; after installing the "
"devel packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:851
#, no-c-format
msgid "GStreamer engine"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:858
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why is there always a gap although I have crossfading enabled?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:862
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure you don't have gst-ffmpeg installed. Instead, install the gst-mad "
"plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I'm getting this error: \"GStreamer-CRITICAL **: Factory for `adder' has no "
"type.\". How to fix?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:873
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your GStreamer was built with Prelinking, which is not compatible with "
"GStreamer. You must rebuild it without this option. merlin-tc advises: <quote>"
"In addition, don't use any ldflags when building GStreamer.</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:881
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You receive an error \"There is no element present to handle the file's "
"mimetype audia/mp4\" even though you have the correct gstreamer-faad plugin is "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:885
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To correctly play mp4 or m4a files with gstreamer, you must also have "
"gstreamer-quicktime in addition to gstreamer-faad installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:892
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You receive an error \"There is no element present to handle the stream's "
"mimetype audio/mpeg\""
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are trying to play an mp3 stream without the gstreamer-mad plugin "
"installed. Install the gstreamer-mad plugin and run \"gst-register\" as root "
"before restarting &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:903
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have a second soundcard and I'm using ALSA. How do I make Amarok use it "
"instead of the default?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>"
"Configure Amarok</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Engine</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
", check the 'Device' checkbox and fill in the device. Typical this is 'hw:0' "
"for the default soundcard, and 'hw:1' for the second soundcard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:918
#, no-c-format
msgid "xine engine"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I change where the audio is output to?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:929
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using ALSA, you can output to a specific device with xine. Set up an "
"~/.asoundrc (user only) or /etc/asound.conf (system wide) file that aliases "
"your hardware devices, and then insert that alias in the \"device used for "
"stereo output:\" box in the xine-engine configuration tab. Alternatively, you "
"can directly enter the alsa device (hw:0,0 or hw:1,0 and so on). If you choose "
"this latter (alternate) method, be aware that ALSA's corresponding plugfoo "
"(e.g. plughw:0,0 or plughw:1,0 and so on) routing through alsa-lib is much "
"preferred."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is a sample ~/.asoundrc for a machine that has an onboard Intel AC97 codec "
"and a usb-audio device:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: faq.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"pcm.intel8x0 {\n"
"          type plug\n"
"          slave.pcm \"hw:0\"\n"
"       }\n"
"      \n"
"       ctl.intel8x0 {\n"
"          type hw\n"
"          card 0\n"
"       }\n"
"       \n"
"       pcm.usb-audio {\n"
"          type plug\n"
"          slave.pcm \"hw:1\"\n"
"       }\n"
"       \n"
"       ctl.usb-audio {\n"
"          type hw\n"
"          card 1\n"
"       }"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now enter usb-audio in the xine-engine setup screen and output should go to the "
"usb-audio device (with alsa-lib properly handling sample rate conversion, "
"channels, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:933
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use a dmixed virtual device, ensure that the \"sound card can do mmap\" "
"checkbox is unchecked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: faq.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid "aRts engine"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: faq.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sorry, aRts-engine has no maintainer, but feel free to fix it yourself! You "
"could be the new aRts-engine maintainer we need so desperately!"
msgstr ""
